          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Generally, a
            %em step function
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            to themselves which is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+function"} constant
            everywhere except at one single point (or a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite number
            of points).
          %p Specifically the function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Θ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi x
                  %mo ↦
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                            %mo &lt;
                            %mn 0
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                            %mo ≥
                            %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Theta \colon x
                  \\mapsto
                  \\left\{
                  \\array{
                  0 &amp;\vert&amp; x \lt 0
                  \\\
                  1 &amp;\vert&amp; x \geq 0
                  }
                  \\right.
          %p
            is sometimes called the
            = succeed "." do
              %em Heaviside step function
          %p
            This may be regarded as the
            = succeed "-expression" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+function"} generalized function
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributional+density"} distributional density
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Θ
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝒟
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Theta \in \mathcal{D}'(\mathbb{R})
            which sends a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bump+function"} bump function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %msubsup
                    %mi C
                    %mi c
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in C^\infty_c(\mathbb{R})
            to its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral"} integral
            over the positive half-axis:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ∫
                            %mi ℝ
                          %mi b
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi Θ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi d
                          %mi x
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≔
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                          %mi Θ
                          %mo ,
                          %mi b
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≔
                          %msubsup
                            %mo ∫
                            %mn 0
                            %mn ∞
                          %mi b
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi d
                          %mi x
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  \\int_{\mathbb{R}} b(x) \Theta(x) d x
                  \&amp; \coloneqq
                  \\langle \Theta, b\rangle
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \coloneqq
                  \\int_0^\infty b(x) d x
                  \\end{aligned}
                  \\,.
          %p
            As such
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Θ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Theta
            is also called the
            = succeed "." do
              %em Heaviside distribution
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivative+of+a+distribution"} distributional derivative
            of the Heaviside distribution is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+delta+distribution"} Dirac delta distribution
            (prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DerivativeOfHeavisideDistribution"}
            below).
          %h2#properties Properties
          #DerivativeOfHeavisideDistribution.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivative+of+distributions"} distributional derivative
              of the Heaviside distribution
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Θ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Theta \in \mathcal{D}'(\mathbb{R})
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delta+distribution"} delta distribution
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi δ
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi 𝒟
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta \in \mathcal{D}'(\mathbb{R})
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi Θ
                    %mo =
                    %mi δ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\partial \Theta = \delta
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %msubsup
                      %mi C
                      %mi c
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in C^\infty_c(\mathbb{R})
              any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bump+function"} bump function
              we compute:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo ∫
                            %mo ∂
                            %mi Θ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi b
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mi d
                            %mi x
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo ∫
                            %mi Θ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ∂
                            %mi b
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mi dx
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %msubsup
                              %mo ∫
                              %mn 0
                              %mn ∞
                            %mo ∂
                            %mi b
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi d
                            %mi x
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mi b
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi x
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %msub
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mrow
                                  %mi x
                                  %mo →
                                  %mn ∞
                              %mo −
                              %mi b
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 0
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi b
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo ∫
                            %mi δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi b
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mi dx
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\int \partial\Theta(x) b(x) \, d x
                    \&amp; =
                    \- \int \Theta(x) \partial b(x)\, dx
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \- \int_0^\infty \partial b(x) d x
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \- \left( b(x)\vert_{x \to \infty} - b(0) \right)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    b(0)
                    \\\
                    \&amp;
                    \=
                    \\int \delta(x) b(x) \, dx
                    \\,.
                    \\end{aligned}
          #FourierIntegralFormula.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+integral"} Fourier integral
                formula for step function)
            %p
              The Heaviside distribution
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Θ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Theta \in \mathcal{D}'(\mathbb{R})
              is equivalently the following
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit+of+a+sequence"} limit
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+integrals"} Fourier integrals
              (see at
              = succeed ")" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+principal+value"} Cauchy principal value
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Θ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mfrac
                              %mn 1
                              %mrow
                                %mn 2
                                %mi π
                                %mi i
                            %msubsup
                              %mo ∫
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn ∞
                              %mn ∞
                            %mfrac
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi e
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi i
                                    %mi ω
                                    %mi x
                              %mrow
                                %mi ω
                                %mo −
                                %mi i
                                %msup
                                  %mn 0
                                  %mo +
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≔
                            %munder
                              %mi lim
                              %mrow
                                %mi ϵ
                                %mo →
                                %msup
                                  %mn 0
                                  %mo +
                            %mfrac
                              %mn 1
                              %mrow
                                %mn 2
                                %mi π
                                %mi i
                            %msubsup
                              %mo ∫
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn ∞
                              %mn ∞
                            %mfrac
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi e
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi i
                                    %mi ω
                                    %mi x
                              %mrow
                                %mi ω
                                %mo −
                                %mi i
                                %mi ϵ
                            %mi d
                            %mi ω
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\Theta(x)
                    \&amp; =
                    \\frac{1}{2\pi i} \int_{-\infty}^\infty \frac{e^{i \omega x}}{\omega - i 0^+}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \coloneqq
                    \\underset{ \epsilon \to 0^+}{\lim}
                    \\frac{1}{2 \pi i}
                    \\int_{-\infty}^\infty \frac{e^{i \omega x}}{\omega - i \epsilon} d\omega
                    \\,,
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              where the limit is taken over
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequences"} sequences
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+numbers"} positive
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon \in (-\infty,0)
              tending to zero.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              We may think of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integrand"} integrand
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi e
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi ω
                            %mi x
                      %mrow
                        %mi ω
                        %mo −
                        %mi i
                        %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{e^{i \omega x}}{\omega - i \epsilon}
              uniquely extended to a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+function"} holomorphic function
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+plane"} complex plane
              and consider computing the given real
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+integral"} line integral
              for fixed
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
              as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contour+integral"} contour integral
              in the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+plane"} complex plane
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in (0,\infty)
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+number"} positive
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mi ω
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi Im
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %mi i
                    %mi Re
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    i \omega x = - Im(\omega) x + i Re(\omega) x
            %div{:style => "float:right;margin:0 10px 10px 0;"}
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/ContoursForHeavisideFourierTransform.png", :width => "300"}/
            %p
              has negative
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+part"} real part
              for
              %em positive
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/imaginary+part"} imaginary part
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+integral"} line integral
              equals the complex
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contour+integral"} contour integral
              over a contour
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo +
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_+ \subset \mathbb{C}
              closing in the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/upper+half+plane"} upper half plane
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \epsilon
              has positive
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/imaginary+part"} imaginary part
              by construction, this contour does encircle the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pole"} pole
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integrand"} integrand
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi e
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi ω
                            %mi x
                      %mrow
                        %mi ω
                        %mo −
                        %mi i
                        %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{e^{i \omega x}}{\omega - i \epsilon}
              at
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ω
                      %mo =
                      %mi i
                      %mi ϵ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega = i \epsilon
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+integral+formula"} Cauchy integral formula
              in the case
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \gt 0
              one gets
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mi lim
                              %mrow
                                %mi ϵ
                                %mo →
                                %msup
                                  %mn 0
                                  %mo +
                            %mfrac
                              %mn 1
                              %mrow
                                %mn 2
                                %mi π
                                %mi i
                            %msubsup
                              %mo ∫
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn ∞
                              %mn ∞
                            %mfrac
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi e
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi i
                                    %mi ω
                                    %mi x
                              %mrow
                                %mi ω
                                %mo −
                                %mi i
                                %mi ϵ
                            %mi d
                            %mi ω
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %munder
                              %mi lim
                              %mrow
                                %mi ϵ
                                %mo →
                                %msup
                                  %mn 0
                                  %mo +
                            %mfrac
                              %mn 1
                              %mrow
                                %mn 2
                                %mi π
                                %mi i
                            %msub
                              %mo ∮
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi C
                                  %mo +
                            %mfrac
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi e
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi i
                                    %mi ω
                                    %mi x
                              %mrow
                                %mi ω
                                %mo −
                                %mi i
                                %mi ϵ
                            %mi d
                            %mi ω
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %munder
                              %mi lim
                              %mrow
                                %mi ϵ
                                %mo →
                                %msup
                                  %mn 0
                                  %mo +
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %msup
                                %mi e
                                %mrow
                                  %mi i
                                  %mi ω
                                  %mi x
                              %msub
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mrow
                                  %mi ω
                                  %mo =
                                  %mi i
                                  %mi ϵ
                              %mo )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %munder
                              %mi lim
                              %mrow
                                %mi ϵ
                                %mo →
                                %msup
                                  %mn 0
                                  %mo +
                            %msup
                              %mi e
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mi ϵ
                                %mi x
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %msup
                              %mi e
                              %mn 0
                            %mo =
                            %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\underset{\epsilon \to 0^+}{\lim}
                    \\frac{1}{2 \pi i}
                    \\int_{-\infty}^\infty \frac{e^{i \omega x}}{\omega - i \epsilon} d\omega
                    \&amp; =
                    \\underset{\epsilon \to 0^+}{\lim}
                    \\frac{1}{2 \pi i}
                    \\oint_{C_+} \frac{e^{i \omega x}}{\omega - i \epsilon} d \omega
                    \\\
                    \&amp;
                    \=
                    \\underset{\epsilon \to 0^+}{\lim}
                    \\left(e^{i \omega x}\vert_{\omega = i \epsilon}\right)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \\underset{\epsilon \to 0^+}{\lim}
                    e^{- \epsilon x}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    e^0 = 1
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Conversely, for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \lt 0
              the real part of the integrand decays as the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/negative+number"} negative
              imaginary part increases, and hence in this case the given line integral equals the contour integral for a contour
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo −
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_- \subset \mathbb{C}
              closing in the lower half plane. Since the integrand has no pole in the lower half plane, in this case the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+integral+formula"} Cauchy integral formula
              says that this integral is zero.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The Fourier form of the step function in prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FourierIntegralFormula"}
              gives rise to the standard expression for the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/advanced+propagator"} advanced propagator
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retarded+propagator"} retarded propagator
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+propagator"} Feynman propagator
              used in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative quantum field theory
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+propagator"} Feynman propagator
              for more.
